        {
         "@type": "meaningComprehension",
         "comprehends": [
          "copies/bb988jx6754.jsonld#inscription-text"
         ],
         "note": "Pencil, faint, written close to the treble edge of the paper so that the tops of the figures run into the edge; read from the lower (180-degree) panel and checked against the upper one. The roll number 369, the day 30 and the year 14 are plain. Between them stand one or two upright strokes with a small entry hook, which could be a single 1 (30.1.14) or a pair 11 (30.11.14); the scan does not carry enough of their heads to decide, so the month is left open. Region 2 shows only a mended perforation, no writing."
        }
       ]
      }
     }
    },
